; pattern-silence — the minimal decode-valid PATTERN container used by the
; B2b dry-run budget negatives: one scalar pattern track carrying
; `(silence)`, so the parity suite can splice a hand-encoded over-budget or
; in-budget body over the single payload record (the same producer bypass
; as `rt_entry` test (p)). The committed pattern-silence.pacb beside this
; file is the REAL CLI's own output; regenerate with
;   zig build run -- pack tools/testdata/pacb/pattern-silence.score.sjon \
;     --out tools/testdata/pacb/pattern-silence.pacb
(target :name radius :arity 1 :registry 0)

(transport :bpm 120 :meter [4 4] :dur 2bar :end loop)

(track :target radius :pattern (silence))
